  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,</p><p>Two sources od same wavelength,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Distance between two sources,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Distance of listener from the source&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>L</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p><p>Condition for minimum intensity, at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>&nbsp;is</p><p>Path difference,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><msqrt><msup><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>n</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>Now, the path difference between the rays is so that the adjacent&nbsp;maxima is obtained,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>.</mo><mi>D</mi><mo>.</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p><p>The path difference between adjacent maxima and minima is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>, form equation (1) and (2) we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>(</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>)</mo></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math></p>",
